#: src/telemetry.md:3
msgid "Telemetry in Zed"
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:5
msgid ""
"Zed collects anonymous telemetry to understand usage patterns and diagnose "
"issues."
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:7
msgid "Telemetry falls into two categories:"
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:9
msgid ""
"**Client-side**: Usage metrics and crash reports. You can disable these in "
"settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:10
msgid ""
"**Server-side**: Collected when using hosted services like AI or "
"Collaboration. Required for these features to function."
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:12
msgid "Configuring Telemetry Settings"
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:14
msgid ""
"You have full control over what data is sent out by Zed. To enable or "
"disable some or all telemetry types, open Settings (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-,|ctrl-,</kbd>) and search for \"telemetry\", or "
"add the following to your settings file:"
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:18
msgid "\"telemetry\""
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:19
msgid "\"diagnostics\""
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:20
msgid "\"metrics\""
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:24
msgid "Dataflow"
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:26
msgid ""
"Telemetry is sent from the application to our servers every 5 minutes (or "
"when 50 events accumulate), then routed to the appropriate service. We "
"currently use:"
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:28
msgid ""
"[Sentry](https://sentry.io): Crash-monitoring service - stores diagnostic "
"events"
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:29
msgid ""
"[Snowflake](https://snowflake.com): Data warehouse - stores both diagnostic "
"and metric events"
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:30
msgid ""
"[Hex](https://www.hex.tech): Dashboards and data exploration - accesses data "
"stored in Snowflake"
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:31
msgid ""
"[Amplitude](https://www.amplitude.com): Dashboards and data exploration - "
"accesses data stored in Snowflake"
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:33
msgid "Types of Telemetry"
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:35
msgid "Diagnostics"
msgstr "診斷"

#: src/telemetry.md:37
msgid ""
"Crash reports consist of a [minidump](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/"
"windows/win32/debug/minidump-files) and debug metadata. Reports are sent on "
"the next launch after a crash, allowing Zed to identify and fix issues "
"without requiring you to file a bug report."
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:39
msgid ""
"You can inspect what data is sent in the `Panic` struct in [crates/"
"telemetry_events/src/telemetry_events.rs](https://github.com/zed-industries/"
"zed/blob/main/crates/telemetry_events/src/telemetry_events.rs). See also: "
"[Debugging Crashes](./development/debugging-crashes.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:41
msgid "Client-Side Metrics"
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:43
msgid "Client-side telemetry includes:"
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:45
msgid "File extensions of opened files"
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:46
msgid "Features and tools used within the editor"
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:47
msgid "Project statistics (e.g., number of files)"
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:48
msgid "Frameworks detected in your projects"
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:50
msgid ""
"This data does not include your code or sensitive project details. Events "
"are sent over HTTPS and rate-limited."
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:52
msgid ""
"Usage data is tied to a random telemetry ID. If you've authenticated, this "
"ID may be linked to your email so Zed can analyze patterns over time and "
"reach out for feedback."
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:54
msgid ""
"To audit what Zed has reported, run <code class=\"hljs\">zed: open telemetry "
"log</code> from the command palette or click `Help > View Telemetry Log`."
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:56
msgid ""
"For the full list of event types, see the `Event` enum in [telemetry_events."
"rs](https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/blob/main/crates/telemetry_events/"
"src/telemetry_events.rs)."
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:58
msgid "Server-Side Metrics"
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:60
msgid ""
"When using Zed's hosted services, we collect metadata for rate limiting and "
"billing (e.g., token usage). Zed does not store your prompts or code unless "
"you explicitly share them via feedback ratings."
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:62
msgid ""
"For details on AI data handling, see [Zed AI Features and Privacy](./ai/ai-"
"improvement.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:64
msgid "Concerns and Questions"
msgstr ""

#: src/telemetry.md:66
msgid ""
"If you have concerns about telemetry, you can [open an issue](https://github."
"com/zed-industries/zed/issues/new/choose) or email hi@zed.dev."
msgstr ""
